Accepted Students Admission & Housing Deposits Orientation Orientation Leaders Transfer Student Orientation Parent & Family Orientation First-Year Student Roadmap Office of New Student Programs Undergraduate Recruitment & Admissions (860) 832-2278 admissions@ccsu.edu Graduate Recruitment & Admissions (860) 832-2350 graduateadmissions@ccsu.edu Breadcrumb Home Accepted Students Admission & Housing Deposits Admission & Housing Deposits For more information or questions about making your deposits, visit the Bursar's Office website . Making Your Deposits Go to the Central Pipeline and log in Click on Student Records and Registration Follow the steps to pay your deposit(s) Admission Deposit New full-time undergraduate students are required to pay a non-refundable $200 enrollment confirmation deposit. This deposit is due by the deadline specified in your admission letter. Housing Deposit To apply for on-campus housing, students are required to complete an online housing application and submit a non-refundable $250 housing deposit. The housing deposit is due by May 1st for Incoming Freshmen and Transfer Students. How to Apply For Housing Important Information Students who are unable to pay the non-refundable housing deposit online may pay their deposit at the Bursar’s Office or mail a check or money order to the Bursar’s Office at: Bursar’s Office CCSU 1615 Stanley Street New Britain, CT 06050 Make the check or money order out to: CCSU. Please make sure you write your student ID number and Housing Deposit on your check or money order. IMPORTANT: If you do mail in the non-refundable housing deposit you MUST still complete an online housing application in order to receive housing. 1615 Stanley Street CT 06050 Directions 860.832.3200 Central Facebook Central Twitter Central Instagram Central Linkedin Central YouTube Contact Us Campus Map Athletics Campus Safety Wellness Services Title IX Search Search Main Navigation (Mobile) Home Admissions First-Year Students Transfer Studen