Menu Human Resources New Employee Information Job Opportunities Hiring Process Hiring and Search Forms Hiring Part-Time Adjuncts Hiring Student Workers Hiring University Assistants Hiring Graduate Assistants Hiring Graduate Interns Hiring and Search Manual Payroll Payroll Overview CORE Self-Service (Time Reporting) Payroll Staff ADA Policy ADA/Reasonable Accommodation Requests Employees and Job Applicants Procedures for Requesting a Reasonable Accommodation Request an Employment Accommodation Students, Guests and Visitors to Central Employee Benefits Education Benefits Employee Assistance Program Family & Medical Leave Medical & Dental Miscellaneous Benefits Retirement Workers' Compensation Part-Time Faculty Information Policies Forms Union Contracts Human Resources Staff Contact Information Human Resources Lawrence J. Davidson Hall 201 (860) 832-1756 humanresources-1@mail.ccsu.edu Payroll Lawrence J. Davidson Hall 211 (860) 832-2525 payroll@mail.ccsu.edu Breadcrumb Home Human Resources Employees and Applicants For Central Job Opportunities Employees and Applicants for Central Job Opportunities Central Human Resources is committed to ensuring that all Central employees and applicants pursing job opportunities receive full and equal opportunity in employment including but not limited to: Hiring, compensation, promotion, training, evaluation or any other term, condition or privilege of employment. The law requires that all employees or persons pursing employment be able to perform the essential functions of their job or jobs for which they apply. Central Human Resources recognizes that some persons may require reasonable accommodations to perform the essential duties related to their job as defined by Central. Therefore, Central Human Resources is committed to providing reasonable accommodation(s) as appropriate. Titles I and II of the ADA, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended, and the Connecticut Discriminatory Practices Act, as amended, prohibit discrimination by state and local government against persons because of their disabilities in governmental programs, services, facilities and employment actions. Central Human Resources recognizes the vital contributions of persons with disabilities in meaningful employment and many activities and programs for which they have historically been excluded. Therefore, Central Human Resources will work collaboratively with any employee or applicant with disabilities seeking an accommodation to identify barriers that may impede meaningful participation, evaluate the necessity of these barriers and will modify or remove non-essential barriers. Most importantly, Central Human Resources will engage in a dialogue with employees or job applicants with disabilities seeking an accommodation to better understand the kinds of barrier removal and other accommodations that might improve their opportunities. To request a reasonable employment accommodation, please visit Employment Accommodation Requests or contact Central Human Resources at 860.832.1756. 1615 Stanley Street CT 06050 Directions 860.832.3200 Central Facebook Central Twitter Central Instagram Central Linkedin Central YouTube Contact Us Campus Map Athletics Campus Safety Wellness Services Title IX Search Search Main Navigation (Mobile) Home Admissions First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Adult/Returning Students Accepted Students Visit Central Tuition & Aid Academics Programs & Majors Departments Schools Register for Classes Calendar Student Support Services Student Life Student Affairs Residence Life Dining & Meal Plans Campus Events Student Activities & Leadership Development About Utility Navigation Apply Visit Give Athletics Calendar Blackboard Central Email Campus Map Courses & Programs Faculty/Staff Directory IT Services News Library"
